## 10. Landing Page — Design & Development Guide

> The landing page is the first impression of ideasUI. It must instantly communicate trust, quality, and ease of use to developers.
> 

---

### Why the Landing Page Matters

| Goal | How ideasUI Achieves It |
| --- | --- |
| Build trust instantly | Clean dark UI, professional typography, live component previews |
| Show value in seconds | Hero tagline + install command above the fold |
| Reduce friction | Copy-paste workflow, no npm install required |
| Drive adoption | Open source badge, GitHub stars, community links |
| Prove quality | Live previews, accessible components, TypeScript support |

---

### Why Use ideasUI?

```
✅ No npm install — just copy the code into your project
✅ Built on Tailwind CSS — works with your existing setup
✅ WAI-ARIA accessible — production-ready out of the box
✅ Dark mode on every component — zero extra config
✅ Full TypeScript support — IntelliSense + type safety
✅ CSS variable theming — match your brand in minutes
✅ Zero runtime dependencies — no bundle size cost
✅ Open source — free forever, community driven
```

---

### Section-Level Design

#### Section 1 — Navbar

```
Logo (ideasUI) | Docs | Components | Examples | [⌘K Search] | [GitHub ★] | [Theme Toggle]
```

- Sticky, `backdrop-blur`, `bg-zinc-950/80` — stays visible on scroll
- GitHub star count badge for social proof
- Keyboard shortcut hint (`⌘K`) builds developer trust

```tsx
<nav className="sticky top-0 z-50 h-16 border-b border-zinc-800 bg-zinc-950/80 backdrop-blur-md">
  <div className="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-6 h-full flex items-center justify-between">
    <Logo />
    <NavLinks /> {/* Docs | Components | Examples */}
    <div className="flex items-center gap-3">
      <SearchTrigger /> {/* ⌘K */}
      <GitHubStars />
      <ThemeToggle />
    </div>
  </div>
</nav>
```

---

#### Section 2 — Hero

> Goal: Communicate the value prop in under 5 seconds.
> 

```
[Badge]     v1.0 — Now Available
[H1]        Build beautiful UIs
            with copy-paste components
[Subtext]   Accessible, customizable, open-source React
            components built with Tailwind CSS.
[Install]   $ npx ideasui init          [Copy]
[CTAs]      [Get Started]  [Browse Components]
```

Design rules:

- Violet gradient glow behind headline (`from-violet-500/10`)
- Headline split: white line 1, `text-violet-400` line 2
- Install command in a pill — monospace, copyable, bordered
- Two CTAs: primary (white bg) + secondary (ghost border)

```tsx
<section className="relative py-28 md:py-40 text-center">
  <div className="absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-b from-violet-500/10 via-transparent to-transparent" />
  <div className="relative max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 space-y-6">
    <Badge>v1.0 — Now Available</Badge>
    <h1 className="text-5xl md:text-7xl font-bold tracking-tight">
      Build beautiful UIs<br />
      <span className="text-violet-400">with copy-paste components</span>
    </h1>
    <p className="text-lg text-zinc-400 max-w-xl mx-auto">
      Accessible, customizable, open-source React components built with Tailwind CSS.
    </p>
    <InstallCommand /> {/* npx ideasui init */}
    <div className="flex gap-3 justify-center">
      <Link href="/docs" className="px-5 py-2.5 rounded-lg bg-white text-black text-sm font-medium hover:bg-zinc-200">Get Started</Link>
      <Link href="/components" className="px-5 py-2.5 rounded-lg border border-zinc-700 text-sm text-zinc-300 hover:bg-zinc-800">Browse Components</Link>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
```

