## 11. Landing Page — Trust, Modern UI, Engaging Content & Responsiveness

---

### 11.1 Building a Trustable UI

Trust is the #1 conversion factor for a component library. Developers won't use a library they don't trust.

#### Trust Signals Checklist

| Signal | Where to Place | Implementation |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Version badge | Hero | `v1.0 — Now Available` pill near headline |
| GitHub stars | Navbar + CTA | Live star count via GitHub API |
| Open source label | Stats bar | `100% Open Source` stat |
| WAI-ARIA badge | Features grid | Accessibility card with shield icon |
| TypeScript badge | Features grid | TypeScript card with type icon |
| "Used by X developers" | Stats / CTA | Social proof number |
| Changelog link | Footer + Navbar | Shows active maintenance |
| MIT License | Footer | `MIT License — Free forever` |

#### Trust-Building Design Rules

```
✅ No broken links or placeholder content on launch
✅ Real component previews — not mockup screenshots
✅ Consistent spacing and alignment throughout
✅ Professional monospace font for all code
✅ Correct syntax highlighting — no errors in code samples
✅ Copy button works on first click
✅ Dark/light toggle works instantly with no flash
✅ All CTAs lead to real pages
```

#### GitHub Stars Widget

```tsx
// Fetch live star count for social proof
async function getGitHubStars(): Promise<number> {
  const res = await fetch("<https://api.github.com/repos/your-org/ideasui>", {
    next: { revalidate: 3600 }, // cache 1 hour
  });
  const data = await res.json();
  return data.stargazers_count ?? 0;
}

// In Navbar
<a href="<https://github.com/your-org/ideasui>"
  className="flex items-center gap-1.5 px-3 py-1.5 rounded-lg border border-zinc-700 text-sm text-zinc-300 hover:bg-zinc-800 transition">
  <Star className="w-3.5 h-3.5 text-yellow-400" />
  {stars.toLocaleString()}
</a>
```

#### Testimonials Section (Social Proof)

> Place between Showcase and Stats. Real quotes from real developers = highest trust signal.
> 

```tsx
const testimonials = [
  {
    quote: "ideasUI saved me hours. Copy, paste, done. No config hell.",
    author: "Sarah K.",
    role: "Frontend Engineer",
    avatar: "/avatars/sarah.jpg",
  },
  {
    quote: "Finally a component lib that doesn't fight my Tailwind setup.",
    author: "Marcus T.",
    role: "Full Stack Developer",
    avatar: "/avatars/marcus.jpg",
  },
  {
    quote: "The accessibility defaults alone are worth switching for.",
    author: "Priya M.",
    role: "UI Engineer",
    avatar: "/avatars/priya.jpg",
  },
];

export default function Testimonials() {
  return (
    <section className="py-20 max-w-5xl mx-auto px-6">
      <h2 className="text-3xl font-bold text-center mb-12">Loved by developers</h2>
      <div className="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
        {testimonials.map(({ quote, author, role, avatar }) => (
          <div key={author} className="p-6 rounded-xl border border-zinc-800 bg-zinc-900/50 space-y-4">
            <p className="text-zinc-300 text-sm leading-relaxed">"{quote}"</p>
            <div className="flex items-center gap-3">
              <img src={avatar} alt={author} className="w-8 h-8 rounded-full object-cover" />
              <div>
                <div className="text-sm font-medium text-white">{author}</div>
                <div className="text-xs text-zinc-500">{role}</div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>
  );
}
```

